X:1
T:Carol of the Bells (Shchedryk)
C:Melody and ostinato: Ukrainian folk chant 'Shchedryk', set by Mykola Leontovych (1916)
O:Ukraine
S:Public-domain material only: the four-note ostinato and the melodic phrases of Leontovych's 'Shchedryk' (1916), checked against a transcription of his choral setting (English Wikipedia article 'Shchedryk (song)'). No English words, and no later arrangement, were used
Z:Arranged and encoded for Go Go HarmoniYo by GitHub Copilot (agent, Claude Opus 5.5), 2026-10-25. The bass and inner parts, the section order, the interlude and the ending are our own.
N:Our own three-voice arrangement for handbells, written from the public-domain Shchedryk material. V:1 lead (ostinato, then the melodic phrases), V:2 inner (sustained chord tones, the ostinato an octave lower, or rests), V:3 bass (our own lines). No dynamics or words.
N:Form (44 bars): intro (ostinato alone, 4) / ostinato over our bass and inner line (8) / upper motif over the low ostinato (4) / descending phrase (4) / rising scale (4) / interlude with pulsing bass (4) / upper motif, phrase, scale again (12) / ostinato and a plain G minor close (4).
N:G minor (B flat, E flat); the rising scale uses E natural and F sharp. Lead range D4-G5, bass C3-A3. Checked: the ostinato is B flat 4 - A4 - B flat 4 - G4 (quarter, two eighths, quarter), octave of every note, and every bar of every voice sums to 3 beats.
